# Python Virtual Environment Rule

- For any Python command in this workspace, use the project virtual environment at `~sharrell/hpcperfstats_monitor_dev/.venv`.
- Prefer direct invocation with `.venv/bin/python` and `.venv/bin/pip` instead of system `python`/`pip`.
- If activation is needed, run `source ~sharrell/hpcperfstats_monitor_dev/.venv/bin/activate` before Python tooling commands.
- Run tests, linters, formatters, scripts, and package installs only through this `.venv`.
- Do not install Python packages globally for this project.
